# Residual RMSNorm pass 2 (e4m3 quantization and transpose): one block of
# 1049 instructions, no branches, no masks, run once by each of the 128
# threads, so every total is exact: per thread 256 f32 flops, 292 B
# loaded and 256 B stored, including the 64 conversions declared inside
# inline-asm scopes. Nothing unknown.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/gluon/quantize_transpose_kernel.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/gluon/quantize_transpose_kernel.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
CHECK: $L__func_begin0  gluon_norm.py:79-99    1049  (end)
CHECK: cvt.rn.satfinite.e4m3x2.f32   64
CHECK: AI(global) = 0.46715328467153283 flop/B
CHECK: unknowns: none
CHECK: coverage: instructions_classified 100.0% (1049/1049)
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry quantize_transpose_kernel( // block 128×1×1 | shared memory 0 B/CTA + dynamic | per CTA: flops f32 32,768; global load 37,376 B, store 32,768 B; shared load 16,384 B, store 16,384 B; param load 5,632 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__func_begin0: // warp * × lane * | exec 128/CTA{{$}}
